* Dijkstra vs Bellman-Ford
** Shortest-path problem
*** Single source, all vertices
*** Shortest-path tree
*** Negative cycle: distance -inf
** Relaxation
*** d(v) > d(u) + w(u,v) => update
*** Upper-bound property
*** Path-relaxation property
** Dijkstra
*** Greedy, settle by distance
*** Priority queue
*** Non-negative weights only
*** O(E + V log V) Fibonacci heap
*** Early exit for one target
** Bellman-Ford
*** Relax all edges, V - 1 passes
*** Any real weights
*** Extra pass detects negative cycle
*** O(VE)
*** Hop-limited paths, SPFA
left side
** Routing
*** Link state: OSPF, IS-IS -> Dijkstra
*** Distance vector: RIP -> Bellman-Ford
*** Count to infinity
** Applications
*** Currency arbitrage (-log rate)
*** Johnson: Bellman-Ford then Dijkstra
*** DAG: topological order, O(V + E)
** Recent results
*** O(m log^(2/3) n), 2025
*** Negative weights near-linear, 2022
